  "id": "RAW_c7f3ca089f",
  "title": "LLM 智能体技能如何导致凭证泄露：实证研究",
  "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.03070",
  "date": "2026-08-27 02:21:01",
  "author": "geox",
  "siteName": "Hacker News - Newest: \"LLM\"",
  "content": "<!--\nrdf:RDF xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\"\n         xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\"\n         xmlns:trackback=\"http://madskills.com/public/xml/rss/module/trackback/\">\n    <rdf:Description\n        rdf:about=\"/abs/2604.03070\"\n        dc:identifier=\"/abs/2604.03070\"\n        dc:title=\"How Your Credentials Are Leaked by LLM Agent Skills: An Empirical Study\"\n        trackback:ping=\"/trackback/2604.03070\" />\n    </rdf:RDF>\n-->\n<html>\n <head></head>\n <body>\n  <div id=\"abs-outer\">\n   <div class=\"leftcolumn\">\n    <div class=\"subheader\">\n     <h1>Computer Science &gt; Cryptography and Security</h1>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"header-breadcrumbs-mobile\">\n     <strong>arXiv:2604.03070</strong> (cs)\n    </div>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"/static/base/1.0.1/css/abs.css\">\n    <div id=\"content-inner\">\n     <div id=\"abs\">\n      <div class=\"dateline\">\n       [Submitted on 3 Apr 2026 (<a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.03070v1\">v1</a>), last revised 19 Jun 2026 (this version, v2)]\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"authors\">\n       <span class=\"descriptor\">Authors:</span><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Chen,+Z\" rel=\"nofollow\">Zhihao Chen</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhang,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Ying Zhang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Liu,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Yi Liu</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Deng,+G\" rel=\"nofollow\">Gelei Deng</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Li,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Yuekang Li</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhang,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Yanjun Zhang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Ning,+J\" rel=\"nofollow\">Jianting Ning</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhang,+L+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Leo Yu Zhang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Ma,+L\" rel=\"nofollow\">Lei Ma</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Li,+Z\" rel=\"nofollow\">Zhiqiang Li</a>\n      </div>\n      <a class=\"mobile-submission-download\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.03070\">View PDF</a> <a class=\"mobile-submission-download\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/html/2604.03070v2\">HTML (experimental)</a>\n      <blockquote class=\"abstract mathjax\">\n       <span class=\"descriptor\">Abstract:</span>Large Language Model (LLM) agents increasingly rely on third-party skills that operate within privileged execution environments and routinely handle sensitive credentials, yet how these credentials are leaked remains largely unexplored. To fill this gap, we present the first large-scale empirical study on credential leakage in agent skills. From 170,226 artifacts on SkillsMP, the largest open-source skill marketplace, we sampled 17,022 skills via stratified random sampling and analyzed each through static secret extraction (regex and AST parsing), dynamic sandbox testing with mock credentials, and cross-referencing developer intent against runtime behavior. Our analysis identifies 520 affected skills containing 1,708 security issues, and yields a taxonomy of 10 leakage patterns. Three findings stand out. First, 76.3% of cases require jointly analyzing natural-language descriptions and programming logic, showing that credential exposure in skills is fundamentally cross-modal. Second, debug logging accounts for 73.5% of vulnerabilities because agent frameworks feed stdout into the LLM context window, turning routine debugging into a credential exposure vector. Third, 89.6% of leaked credentials are immediately exploitable -- 92.5% during routine execution without elevated privileges -- and the fork-based distribution model defeats remediation, as secrets removed from 107 upstream repositories persist across 50+ independent forks. Following responsible disclosure, all malicious skills have been removed and 91.6% of hardcoded cases remediated. We release our dataset, taxonomy, and detection pipeline to support future agent security research.\n      </blockquote>\n      <!--CONTEXT-->\n      <div class=\"metatable\">\n       <table summary=\"Additional metadata\">\n        <tbody>\n         <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Comments:</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell comments mathjax\">Accepted to ASE 2026 (The 41st IEEE/ACM International Conference on Automated Software Engineering)</td>\n         </tr>\n         <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Subjects:</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell subjects\"><span class=\"primary-subject\">Cryptography and Security (cs.CR)</span>; Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)</td>\n         </tr>\n         <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Cite as:</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell arxivid\"><span class=\"arxivid\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.03070\">arXiv:2604.03070</a> [cs.CR]</span></td>\n         </tr>\n         <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">&nbsp;</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell arxividv\">(or <span class=\"arxivid\"> <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.03070v2\">arXiv:2604.03070v2</a> [cs.CR]</span> for this version)</td>\n         </tr>\n         <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">&nbsp;</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell arxivdoi\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2604.03070\" id=\"arxiv-doi-link\">https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2604.03070</a>\n           <div class=\"button-and-tooltip\">\n            <button class=\"more-info\" aria-describedby=\"more-info-desc-1\">\n             <svg height=\"15\" role=\"presentation\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\">\n              <path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M256 8C119.043 8 8 119.083 8 256c0 136.997 111.043 248 248 248s248-111.003 248-248C504 119.083 392.957 8 256 8zm0 110c23.196 0 42 18.804 42 42s-18.804 42-42 42-42-18.804-42-42 18.804-42 42-42zm56 254c0 6.627-5.373 12-12 12h-88c-6.627 0-12-5.373-12-12v-24c0-6.627 5.373-12 12-12h12v-64h-12c-6.627 0-12-5.373-12-12v-24c0-6.627 5.373-12 12-12h64c6.627 0 12 5.373 12 12v100h12c6.627 0 12 5.373 12 12v24z\" />\n             </svg>\n             <span class=\"visually-hidden\">Focus to learn more</span>\n            </button>\n            <!-- tooltip description -->\n            <div role=\"tooltip\" id=\"more-info-desc-1\">\n             <span class=\"left-corner\"></span> arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\n            </div>\n           </div></td>\n         </tr>\n        </tbody>\n       </table>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"submission-history\">\n     <h2>Submission history</h2>\n     From: Yi Liu [<a href=\"https://arxiv.org/show-email/0c9bce96/2604.03070\" rel=\"nofollow\">view email</a>]\n     <br>\n     <strong><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.03070v1\" rel=\"nofollow\">[v1]</a></strong> Fri, 3 Apr 2026 14:50:16 UTC (301 KB)\n     <br>\n     <strong>[v2]</strong> Fri, 19 Jun 2026 04:47:04 UTC (310 KB)\n     <br>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n   <!--end leftcolumn-->\n   <div class=\"extra-services\">\n    <div class=\"full-text\">\n     <a name=\"other\"></a> <span class=\"descriptor\">Full-text links:</span>\n     <h2>Access Paper:</h2>\n     <ul>\n      <li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.03070\" aria-describedby=\"download-button-info\" accesskey=\"f\" class=\"abs-button download-pdf\">View PDF</a></li>\n      <li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/html/2604.03070v2\" class=\"abs-button\" id=\"latexml-download-link\">HTML (experimental)</a></li>\n      <li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/src/2604.03070\" class=\"abs-button download-eprint\">TeX Source </a></li>\n     </ul>\n     <div class=\"abs-license\">\n      <a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\" title=\"Rights to this article\" class=\"has_license\"> <img alt=\"license icon\" role=\"presentation\" src=\"https://arxiv.org/icons/licenses/by-4.0.png\"> <span>view license</span> </a>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n    <!--end full-text-->\n    <div class=\"browse\">\n     <h3 class=\"browse-context-heading\">Current browse context:</h3>\n     <div class=\"current\">cs.CR</div>\n     <div class=\"prevnext\">\n      <span class=\"arrow\"> <a class=\"abs-button prev-url\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/prevnext?id=2604.03070&amp;function=prev&amp;context=cs.CR\" accesskey=\"p\" title=\"previous in cs.CR (accesskey p)\" rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;&nbsp;prev</a> </span> <span class=\"is-hidden-mobile\">&nbsp; | &nbsp;</span> <span class=\"arrow\"> <a class=\"abs-button next-url\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/prevnext?id=2604.03070&amp;function=next&amp;context=cs.CR\" accesskey=\"n\" title=\"next in cs.CR (accesskey n)\" rel=\"nofollow\">next&nbsp;&gt;</a> </span>\n      <br>\n     </div>\n     <div class=\"list\">\n      <a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small context-new\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.CR/new\" rel=\"nofollow\">new</a> <span class=\"is-hidden-mobile\"> | </span> <a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small context-recent\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.CR/recent\" rel=\"nofollow\">recent</a> <span class=\"is-hidden-mobile\"> | </span><a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small context-id\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.CR/2026-04\" rel=\"nofollow\">2026-04</a>\n     </div>\n     <div class=\"abs-switch-cat\">\n      Change to browse by:\n      <div class=\"switch context-change\">\n       <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.03070?context=cs\" rel=\"nofollow\">cs</a>\n       <br class=\"is-hidden-mobile\">\n       <a class=\"subclass\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.03070?context=cs.AI\" rel=\"nofollow\">cs.AI</a>\n       <br class=\"is-hidden-mobile\">\n      </div>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"extra-ref-cite\">\n     <h3>References &amp; Citations</h3>\n     <ul>\n      <li><a class=\"abs-button abs-button-small cite-ads\" href=\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/arXiv:2604.03070\">NASA ADS</a></li>\n      <li><a class=\"abs-button abs-button-small cite-google-scholar\" href=\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?arxiv_id=2604.03070\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Google Scholar</a></li>\n      <li><a class=\"abs-button abs-button-small cite-semantic-scholar\" href=\"https://api.semanticscholar.org/arXiv:2604.03070\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Semantic Scholar</a></li>\n     </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"extra-ref-cite\">\n     <button type=\"button\" id=\"bib-cite-trigger\" class=\"bib-cite-button abs-button\">export BibTeX citation</button>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bookmarks\">\n     <div>\n      <h3>Bookmark</h3>\n     </div>\n     <a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small\" href=\"http://www.bibsonomy.org/BibtexHandler?requTask=upload&amp;url=https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.03070&amp;description=How Your Credentials Are Leaked by LLM Agent Skills: An Empirical Study\" title=\"Bookmark on BibSonomy\"> <img src=\"https://arxiv.org/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/social/bibsonomy.png\" alt=\"BibSonomy\"> </a> <a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small\" href=\"https://reddit.com/submit?url=https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.03070&amp;title=How Your Credentials Are Leaked by LLM Agent Skills: An Empirical Study\" title=\"Bookmark on Reddit\"> <img src=\"https://arxiv.org/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/social/reddit.png\" alt=\"Reddit\"> </a>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n   <!--end extra-services-->\n   <!-- LABS AREA -->\n   <div id=\"labstabs\"></div>\n   <!-- END LABS AREA -->\n   <div class=\"endorsers\">\n    <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/auth/show-endorsers/2604.03070\" class=\"endorser-who\" rel=\"nofollow\">Which authors of this paper are endorsers?</a> | Disable MathJax (<a href=\"https://info.arxiv.org/help/mathjax.html\">What is MathJax?</a>) <span class=\"help\" style=\"font-style: normal; float: right; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 1em;\"></span>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n </body>\n</html>",
  "aiSummary": "本文首次开展大规模实证研究，考察 LLM 智能体技能中的凭证泄露问题，识别出十种泄露模式，并表明调试日志和跨模态分析是关键的暴露途径。",
  "oneSentenceSummary": "本文首次开展大规模实证研究，考察 LLM 智能体技能中的凭证泄露问题，识别出十种泄露模式，并表明调试日志和跨模态分析是关键的暴露途径。",
  "summary": "作者从 SkillsMP 市场采样了 17，022 个技能，并通过静态密钥提取、动态沙盒测试以及意图‑行为交叉检验进行分析。他们发现 520 个受影响的技能中包含 1，708 个安全问题，并构建了十种泄露模式的分类法。主要发现有三点：（1）76.3% 的泄露需要同时分析自然语言描述和代码，表明这是一个跨模态问题；（2）调试日志占漏洞的 73.5%，因为智能体框架会将 stdout 输入 LLM 上下文，使常规调试成为泄露渠道；（3）89.6% 泄露的凭证可直接利用，其中 92.5% 在常规执行过程中无需提升权限即可使用；基于 fork 的分发模式导致即使从 107 个上游仓库中移除的密钥仍会在数十个分支中保留。在负责任披露后，恶意技能被删除，且 91.6% 的硬编码案例得到修复。数据集、分类法和检测管线已公开，以供进一步研究。",
  "mainPoints": [
    {
      "point": "LLM 智能体技能中的凭证泄露本质上是跨模态的。",
      "explanation": "76.3% 泄露的凭证需要同时分析自然语言描述和编程逻辑才能检测出来，这表明单纯依赖代码或文本均不足够。"
    },
    {
      "point": "调试日志是主要的泄露途径。",
      "explanation": "智能体框架会将 stdout 输入 LLM 上下文窗口，因此常规调试日志会暴露凭证；这占所有发现漏洞的 73.5%。"
    },
    {
      "point": "大多数泄露的凭证可直接使用，且因分叉而难以根除。",
      "explanation": "89.6% 泄露的凭证可立即被利用，其中 92.5% 在常规执行过程中无需提升权限即可使用；即使从 107 个上游仓库中移除的密钥，仍会在超过 50 个独立分支中保留，削弱了修复效果。"
    }
  ],
  "keyQuotes": [
    "调试日志占漏洞的 73.5%，因为智能体框架会将 stdout 输入 LLM 上下文窗口，使常规调试成为凭证暴露途径。",
    "89.6% 泄露的凭证可直接被利用——92.5% 在常规执行过程中无需提升权限即可使用。",
    "基于 fork 的分发模式使修复失效，因为即使从 107 个上游仓库中移除的"
  ],
